Hyphenation dictionaries in this directory
==========================================

Two stock pattern sets, redistributed under their own terms, and one file of
bokai's own. Each pattern file repeats its licence in its own header; this
file records where each came from and what was changed.


hyph_en_US.dic — American English
---------------------------------

From the LibreOffice dictionaries collection, `en/hyph_en_US.dic`, verbatim.

    https://github.com/LibreOffice/dictionaries

BSD-style: unlimited copying, redistribution and modification are permitted
with the copyright and licence information the file carries. It is the plain
TeX hyphenation table (`hyphen.tex`, Copyright Donald E. Knuth) together with
the TUGboat hyphenation exception log (Copyright 2007 TeX Users Group, freely
usable, modifiable and distributable), converted by László Németh.


hyph_de_1996.dic — German, reformed (1996) orthography
------------------------------------------------------

From the `hyph-utf8` distribution of TeX hyphenation patterns, pattern list
`hyph-de-1996.pat.txt`.

    https://github.com/hyphenation/tex-hyphen

MIT, Copyright (c) 2013-2024 Stephan Hennig, Werner Lemberg, Günter Milde,
Sander van Geloven, Georg Pfeiffer, Gisbert W. Selke, Tobias Wendorf and Keno
Wehr, by the Deutschsprachige Trennmustermannschaft. The full notice is in the
file's own header.

Changed: a `UTF-8` character set line and the `LEFTHYPHENMIN` /
`RIGHTHYPHENMIN` keywords, so that a pattern list reads as a libhyphen
dictionary. The values are the typesetting minimums the source states. No
pattern is altered, added or removed.


en.curation — English break decisions
-------------------------------------

bokai's own, under the licence of the crate. It states nothing about any other
dictionary and is derived from none: it is a list of words with the breaks
chosen for them by hand, and the file explains what those choices are for.
